$X$ is guaranteed to be a factorial of some integer $N$.

Approach:
Since $N!$ grows very rapidly, $N$ will be relatively small for the given constraint on $X$.
Let's estimate the maximum value of $N$.
$20! \approx 2.4 \times 10^{18}$.
$21! \approx 5.1 \times 10^{19}$.
Since $X \le 3 \times 10^{18}$, $N$ will be at most 20.
Actually, let's check $20!$.
