$21! \approx 5.1 \times 10^{19}$.
So $N$ is in the range $[1, 20]$ (or maybe slightly higher if constraints were larger, but here max $X$ is $3 \times 10^{18}$, so $N \le 20$).
Wait, the constraint says $X \le 3 \times 10^{18}$.
$20! \approx 2.43 \times 10^{18}$.
$21! \approx 5.1 \times 10^{19}$.
So $N$ is indeed $\le 20$.

Since the range of possible $N$ is very small, we can simply iterate through integers $i = 1, 2, 3, \dots$ and calculate $i!$. If $i! = X$, we print $i$ and stop. If $i! > X$, we stop (though the problem guarantees a solution exists).

